cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Nmahjong, please cite it as below."
title: "Nmahjong: data formats for N-tile mahjong (tileset, ruleset, wall, record, annotation) with reference implementations"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ohba-artlife"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ohba-artlife/Nmahjong"
keywords:
  - mahjong
  - riichi mahjong
  - game record
  - data format
  - reference implementation
abstract: >-
  Nmahjong defines five layers of data for mahjong generalised by the set of tiles,
  the hand size N and the number of players M: tileset, ruleset, wall, record and annotation.
  Every object is identified by the SHA-256 hash of its canonical JSON.
  A reference implementation in Python and a second implementation in JavaScript
  create, verify and replay these data, judge winning hands, and run games;
  46 rulesets written from published rule texts are bundled.
